f these serve as additional baselines?\n\n5. **Constrained decoding literature**: Is the log-prob compression observation truly novel? Has anyone in the grammar-guided generation community noted this?\n\n6. **Significance of contributions**: Are the contributions sufficient for Findings? Would a main conference accept this?\n\n7. **Writing quality and clarity**: Is the paper well-written? Is the narrative compelling?\n\n8. **Scope and generalizability**: How broadly do these findings apply? Only to JSON-schema IE? Other structured generation tasks (code, SQL)?\n\nFormat your review as:\n```\n## R2 Review: Novelty and Related Work\n\n### Summary (2-3 sentences)\n\n### Strengths\n- S1: ...\n- S2: ...\n(etc.)\n\n### Weaknesses\n- W1: ...\n- W2: ...\n(etc.)\n\n### Questions for Authors\n- Q1: ...\n(etc.)\n\n### Minor Issues\n- ...\n\n### Preliminary Scores\n- Soundness: X/5\n- Excitement: X/5\n- Reproducibility: X/5\n- Overall: X/5\n- Confidence: X/5\n```\n\nBe rigorous but fair. Focus on whether the contribution is genuinely novel and significant for the EMNLP Findings audience.\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GJcwQEcAFdZugRUsDbxRDD","session_id":"8860f592-6591-47fa-b978-f5709a359b4d","uuid":"066c877b-9cff-4519-bff1-72f5686088eb","timestamp":"2026-05-15T10:07:52.091Z"}
