 specified\\\\n      coverage levels. Theoretical foundation for our consistency-based selective prediction in IE.'\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch3\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T19:30:00.000Z'\\\\n  ren2023selfevaluation:\\\\n    title: Self-Evaluation Improves Selective Generation in Large Language Models\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Jie Ren\\\\n    - Yao Zhao\\\\n    - Tu Vu\\\\n    - Peter J. Liu\\\\n    - Balaji Lakshminarayanan\\\\n    year: 2023\\\\n    venue: NeurIPS 2023 Workshop\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.09300\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    bibtex_key: ren2023selfevaluation\\\\n    category: selective_prediction\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    relevance: Proposes LLM self-evaluation for selective generation, reformulating open-ended tasks into token-level predictions\\\\n      to leverage better calibration. Directly relevant to our confidence-aware abstention mechanism for structured IE.\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch3\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T19:30:00.000Z'\\\\n  wadhwa2023revisiting:\\\\n    title: Revisiting Relation Extraction in the era of Large Language Models\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Somin Wadhwa\\\\n    - Silvio Amir\\\\n    - Byron Wallace\\\\n    year: 2023\\\\n    venue: ACL 2023\\\\n    url: https://aclanthology.org/2023.acl-long.868/\\\\n    doi: 10.18653/v1/2023.acl-long.868\\\\n    bibtex_key: wadhwa2023revisiting\\\\n    category: generative_ie\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    relevance: 'Foundation paper: evaluates LLMs (GPT-3, Flan-T5) for relation extraction as seq2seq, showing few-shot prompting\\\\n      achieves near-SOTA performance. Establishes generative RE paradigm our structured consistency method builds upon.'\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch4\\\\n    added_a